attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a short spine.** Columns 0 to 2, `yicS` to `yicL`, are carried by 97 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 0.2 to 2% of calls {S1, P}. The model names 95 to 99% of them, fewest at column 1, `nlpA`, 95% {S1}.

@variable **A fork follows at `setC`**, column 3, carried by 73%, with a second family in 32% {S2.c3}. Then columns 4 to 15, `yicJ` to `yicG`, are the stretch most in regions of plasticity, 29 to 50%, [[lipopolysaccharide core]] {S3, P, Q}. Through columns 32 to 36 a branch of 5 shell families runs in 16%, [[lipopolysaccharide]] {S8.b32, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 85 against 82%, and hesitates more there, 0.71 against 0.41 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 4, `yicJ`, a spine column, 2.66 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends in variable columns.** Columns 67 to 79, `yibF` to `ulaD`, are carried by 7 to 62% {S8.c67-79}. The last column is `ulaD`, in 18% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 83% of genes**, 0.52 bits on average, perplexity 2.2 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.22 against 0.20 bits, and names fewer genes, 61% against 93% {C}.

